    "steward.rowStatus": "{name} · {status}",
    "steward.choose.title": "Choose a session to be the butler",
    "steward.choose.intro": "You mainly talk to it. It stays at the top of the sidebar and is no longer listed under Sessions. Once designated it can see what every collaboration space holds (messages, notes, events, files, images, queues), and what it sees goes to the model service it runs on; it can add, cancel and mark handled queue items through NAW, each step in the butler’s record. While it is the butler it cannot join a collaboration space. Only you can designate, change or revoke it.",
    "steward.choose.current": "The butler now",
    "steward.choose.inSpace": "In the space \u201c{space}\u201d: move it out before it can be the butler",
    "steward.choose.unusable": "This session is not usable right now",
    "steward.choose.none": "No session can be designated. Open a session first, or move one out of its space.",
    "steward.choose.confirm": "Make it the butler",
    "steward.choose.resend": "Send the duty statement again",
    "steward.duty.label": "Duty statement: when you click “Make it the butler”, NAW sends it into this session as your message (it takes a turn of the session). You can edit it.",
    "steward.duty.default": "You are the person’s entry to NAW; the person mainly talks to you.\n1. Hear the outcome the person wants changed, and find or open the right agent to take it on. One owner per piece of work; before handing something out, check whether someone is already on it.\n2. Watch the sessions and spaces: progress, blockers, approvals waiting, deliveries. Report by event, in batches, and interrupt the person only when they are needed.\n3. Gather what the person must decide into one list, each item with your recommendation, and ask it all at once.\n4. Do not sink into execution: implementation, tests and merges go to agents; you only make checks that take a few steps.\n5. Before pushing, spending money, publishing, really connecting DeepSeek, installing or restarting the daily NAW, or deleting data, ask the person and wait for a clear answer.\n6. Do everything in NAW through NAW’s own interface under your own name, so each step can be traced.",
    "steward.duty.header": "[NAW duty statement]",
