    "butler.reads.title": "What the butler has read",
    "butler.reads.intro": "Each time the butler looks up a queue, delivery records or the list of spaces, that is one page (at most {limit} items; a lookup that finds nothing still counts), and it leaves one line here: when, which kind, which space, how many came back. No content is kept. Space names are matched to the spaces you have now; the log stores ids only. Pages withheld for lack of capacity still count toward the daily 64 pages, even though they were not sent to the model; reads refused before execution do not count.",
    "butler.reads.limits": "A line means NAW approved giving the page to the butler (every page is logged before it is given), and does not show that the model service received it. The log is not tamper-proof: any program running under your account can delete or change it, and deleting it or changing the system clock gets around the limit of {limit} pages a day.",
